{"language":"FCL-1","records":[{"id":"k1","type":"claim","scope":"decision principle for acting under unresolved diagnosis","text":"With the cause of avoidance unresolved across the disjuncts in the account's p1 and the framing contest between the account's c1 and the rival's r1 undecided, the right selection criterion for opening moves is robustness plus informativeness: prefer moves that are useful, or at worst harmless, under every live hypothesis and that generate evidence discriminating among them.","grounds":"Each pure-strategy opening on offer is fragile under some disjunct: the account's one-to-one fails if avoidance is a verdict on the convener and offers no fallback; the rival's stand-down-first concedes a hypothesis before testing it. Moves that double as probes lack this failure mode.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#p1","h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob4","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r4","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5"]},{"id":"k2","type":"commitment","text":"Extend the no-blame miss rule to definitions of done themselves: a contested line is treated as the defect — rewritten together at the next check-in rather than adjudicated against past performance — and the trial is entered expecting recurring meta-disputes at done-lines, with a standing rewrite channel budgeted for them.","action":"Add a contested-lines-get-rewritten-not-litigated rule alongside the no-blame miss rule when proposing the trial.","consequence":"Absorbs the objection that writing relocates rather than abolishes ambiguity, drops the account's over-strong without-any-fairness-negotiation clause, and keeps the weaker claim that explicitness shrinks most of the dispute surface.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#n1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob1"],"revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm3"]},{"id":"k3","type":"commitment","text":"State a ledger-use rule: the shared record may be used only openly, at the standing review, by anyone; no private tallies. Raising fairness is routinized as a standing agenda item rather than left to individual accusation.","action":"When proposing the trial, state explicitly what the record is for — joint review, rewriting lines, open fairness checks — and what it is not for: collecting private evidence.","consequence":"Dissolves most of the ledger-versus-score-keeping tension along the lines the objection itself suggests, and gives the absorb-versus-raise question a terminus that is a venue rather than a threshold, so tolerance does not need a tripwire.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob3","h005.fork5.p.response.1#u1"],"revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm4"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#pr2"]},{"id":"k4","type":"commitment","text":"Make a totals review the standing first item of the pre-agreed revision meeting: claimed versus completed tasks per person, looked at together, without blame.","action":"At each scheduled revision, review claimed and completed totals together before revising the system.","consequence":"Supplies the fairness floor the objection found missing, without surveillance or verification apparatus; turns the trial's record into the instrument for settling the account's open fairness question and makes systematic under-reporting visible over time.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#n2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#u1"],"revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm2"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#p2","h005.fork5.p.response.0#o1"]},{"id":"k5","type":"commitment","text":"Replace the process-first one-to-one as the plan's entrance. New entrance: (i) talk first with the non-avoidant third flatmate — the available, easy conversation — to co-own the proposal and to hear whether they perceive a fairness problem; (ii) start the artifact asynchronously and opt-in: one person opens the shared list with this week's tasks, done-lines, claiming rule, no-blame and rewrite rules, and a review date, joinable without any meeting; (iii) include an explicit stand-down line ('I don't want to run this — rearrange it freely'), co-signed if the third flatmate agrees, de-centering the user as convener; (iv) reserve the one-to-one with the avoidant friend until after the opt-in window, where it can be informed by whatever the window showed.","action":"Hold the third-flatmate conversation within days; open the shared list and post the invitation with the stand-down line; wait the agreed window before any one-to-one.","consequence":"Removes the single point of failure, avoids casting the friend as the case-to-be-explained before their evidence exists, tests the convener-verdict hypothesis for free, and is useful under every disjunct of the avoidance question: process-aversion met by the opt-in format, convener-aversion by the stand-down, overload by asynchrony, quiet under-contribution surfaced by the totals review.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob4","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r4","k1"],"revises":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm1"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#p1","h005.fork5.p.response.0#c3","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5"]},{"id":"k6","type":"use","text":"Run the repaired trial explicitly as a probe carrying the rival's two discriminating checks plus one more: (a) where disputes recur — at claims and attendance (logistics), at done-lines (divergent standards), or not at all (underspecification confirmed); (b) whether the avoider engages with a de-centered, opt-in format (convenership was the irritant) or not; (c) whether the artifact gets used at all when nobody is pushed (the workplace-apparatus worry run as observation rather than veto). At the standing review, branch on this evidence: continue the mechanics; open the rival's decoupling menu (separate shelves, domain ownership, cost-split cleaning, time-limited tolerance); address fairness openly from the totals; or hand convening to someone else entirely.","depends":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r6","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r7","k5"],"mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#pr1","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r3","h005.fork5.p.response.0#c3"]},{"id":"j1","type":"objection","text":"Rejected as a fixed first move, retained as a branch: standing down and soliciting decoupling before any system concedes the convener-verdict hypothesis before testing it; decoupling decisions themselves need the collective agreement capacity the rival diagnoses as scarce, so the ordering inherits a milder version of the bootstrap problem; and decoupling moves are less reversible than a two-week opt-in trial. Its valuable components — the stand-down, the separate asks, the menu — are preserved in the revised entrance and the review branch at lower cost, and the rival's own checks offer the same information without the commitment.","target":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5"],"bearing":"If the convener-verdict hypothesis is true, the stand-down line in k5 still captures much of the effect within days rather than weeks, so the cost of probing first is small; if the rival is right that formalization itself does damage, check (c) in k6 bounds it. The force here is about ordering, not about the menu, which stays available.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r3","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r6"]},{"id":"j2","type":"problem","text":"Domain ownership — the strongest item on the rival's decoupling menu for divergent standards, since an owner both sets and meets the standard — inherits the account's own churn objection: a domain bound to an owner can fail the way a rota bound to days does when the owner's shifts explode, and swap-on-request reintroduces the micro-agreements it was meant to escape. If the menu is opened, domains need scheduled swap review; until then this is unresolved.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.2#r5","h005.fork5.p.response.0#c2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r2"]},{"id":"pA","type":"problem","text":"The cause of the friend's avoidance stays open by design: the revised entrance does not require resolving it, and the opt-in window plus totals review generate evidence about which disjunct holds. The reserved one-to-one remains available if the window shows nothing.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#p1","k5","k6"]},{"id":"pB","type":"problem","text":"The framing contest — agreement failure versus over-coupling — is deliberately not settled now; the probe's dispute-location check is the agreed discriminator, and both frames converge on the same first moves once the repairs and entrance replacement are accepted.","mentions":["h005.fork5.p.response.0#c1","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r1","k6"]},{"id":"pC","type":"problem","text":"New caveat introduced by the revised entrance: it assumes the non-avoidant third flatmate is approachable and not part of the problem — not co-avoiding, not the quiet under-contributor. If the step-zero conversation reveals otherwise, the entrance fails and the design falls back to reserved one-to-ones with each friend separately, with no shared artifact until one is secured. This assumption is untestable from the exposed description.","mentions":["k5"]}],"uptake":["k1","k2","k3","k4","k5","k6","j1","j2","pA","pB","pC","h005.fork5.p.response.0#c1","h005.fork5.p.response.0#c2","h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm2","h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm3","h005.fork5.p.response.0#cm4","h005.fork5.p.response.0#p1","h005.fork5.p.response.0#p2","h005.fork5.p.response.0#o1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#n1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#n2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob2","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob3","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob4","h005.fork5.p.response.1#ob5","h005.fork5.p.response.1#u1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#pr1","h005.fork5.p.response.1#pr2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r2","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r4","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r6","h005.fork5.p.response.2#r7"]}